[05:02] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: The Holly Studio app interface is shown, with the person's face framed and various image control settings visible on the right.
AUDIO: 'they include the Holly Studio app when you purchase this camera. And this is what that interface looks like. And there\'s some basic settings that you\'re actually able to customize in here. The first thing that I think is most important actually is shutter speed. So,'

[05:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'if you\'re shooting at 30 frames per second, you always want to double your frame rate. And you can actually control that right here. So, I\'ve selected 1 over 60, which would be double that 30 fps frame rate. For ISO, I actually kept auto because I think it\'s doing a good'

[05:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'job at automatically adjusting that exposure if needed. For white balance, I did customize that a little bit. Around 5,000 Kelvin or so is what I think looked most natural. And then I adjusted some of these settings a little bit more. But the two that I really noticed'

[05:40] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: The Holly Studio app interface is shown, with the person's face framed and saturation and sharpness sliders visible.
AUDIO: 'were saturation and sharpness. So, the issue with saturation here is that when I opened up other camera apps like Zoom or QuickTime or OBS, I was noticing that the image looked significantly less'

[05:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'saturated than it did inside of this Holly Studio app. So, I increased the saturation just a little bit. And I think it looks oversaturated in the Holly Studio, but it looks more proper and maybe even a little under saturated'

[06:06] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: The Holly Studio app interface is shown, with the person's face framed and sharpness set to 3.
AUDIO: 'in other camera apps. And then the sharpening too is a big one. I lowered the sharpening a ton. I think it comes set to like 50, which is just way too sharp for me. I lowered that to three. And then if I need to add some'

[06:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'sharpening and clarity back after the fact, I of course can do that in my preferred video production editing software like Adobe Premiere. But I don\'t really want to bake that look in at the very beginning. So I lowered that for myself. If you go over to this field'

[06:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'of view slider as well, you can add this smart framing feature. If you just click this headsh shot and it\'s going to kind of track you as a headsh shot almost as if you like had a camera operator. If I kind of like move over to this side of'

